# Cloudflare Pages security headers, applied to every route.
#
# CSP ships REPORT-ONLY on purpose: Astro inlines the small island scripts
# (<script type="module"> in the built HTML), which `script-src 'self'` will FLAG in a
# browser's console without blocking anything. Before promoting to an enforcing
# Content-Security-Policy, externalize or hash those inline scripts and confirm zero
# violations in DevTools. Report-only cannot break the site; enforcing can, silently.
#
# Violations are reported to /api/csp-report, a Pages Function that logs a DIRECTIVE NAME
# and an ORIGIN-ONLY blocked URI and persists nothing. See functions/api/csp-report.js
# for the five constraints it is built to, and /privacy, which discloses the collection.
#
# BOTH `report-uri` and `report-to` are set, deliberately. `report-uri` is deprecated but
# broadly supported; `report-to` is its replacement and needs the Reporting-Endpoints
# header below. Per MDN (checked 2026-09-10): a browser that supports `report-to` IGNORES
# `report-uri`, so the pair is a fallback and not double-reporting. A report you never
# receive is indistinguishable from a violation that never happened, so the compatible
# form is the safe one while the policy is still being observed.
#
# HSTS (Strict-Transport-Security) is intentionally NOT set here — it stays a Cloudflare
# dashboard toggle (founder's call).
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Reporting-Endpoints: csp-endpoint="/api/csp-report"
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; img-src 'self' data:; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; form-action 'self'; report-uri /api/csp-report; report-to csp-endpoint
